      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`ExaoneMoEForCausalLM` never set `model_runner.sliding_window_size`, so the triton backend built no window buffers and every sliding layer failed at kernel compile (`kv_indptr is None`). The window passed to `RadixAttention` was also one too large: HF counts the query token inside the window, SGLang counts only the earlier tokens (`exaone4.py` and `gemma3_causal.py` already subtract one).\n\nPart 1 of the K-EXAONE 1.0 serving stack. (I'll continuously support EXAONE for SGLang) \n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add a module-level `get_attention_sliding_window_size(config)` returning `config.sliding_window - 1` and use it for the `RadixAttention` window on sliding layers.\n- Expose the same value through `ExaoneMoEForCausalLM.get_attention_sliding_window_size()` so the attention backends build their window buffers.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n16x A100 40GB, bf16, TP16, `--attention-backend triton`: before this change the server fails at the first sliding layer; after it, generation is coherent at 400 tokens. With the follow-up MTP-head change (It will be part 2) MTP acceptance is 0.880 (gsm8k) / 0.737 (mt-bench), GSM8K 90.0 (1319, non-thinking).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable (correctness fix; no kernel or scheduling change).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (the window value is asserted by the unit test added in part 2)\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38067840426](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38067840426)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38067840261](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38067840261)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38067840463](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38067840463)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
